   231	### 2.4 Shifted Theorem 5.1 and Corollary 5.3
   232	
   233	For a complete final-major partition, Moh's printed p.171 formula gives
   234	
   235	\[
   236	 -\lambda_Q={n(1+\ell-\delta_\sigma)\over n-M_1}
   237	 ={n\over n+m}(1+\ell-\delta_\sigma),
   238	\]
   239	
   240	because \(M_1=-m\). Minor roots have order zero. The monic root product in
   241	§1 therefore proves
   242	
   243	\[
   244	 \boxed{I(P'_\xi,Q')=I_M^\ell(P',Q')
   245	 ={n\over n+m}\sum_{\sigma\in\mathcal P_M}
   246	 |D^{P'_\xi}_\sigma|(1+\ell-\delta_\sigma).}
   247	\]
   248	
   249	This is a sum over actual final discs and actual root cardinalities. Individual
   250	summands may be fractional; the complete sum is the resultant degree and must
   251	be integral. Combining it with §2.3 gives
   252	
   253	\[
   254	 I_M^\ell\ge I_m^\ell+k\ge I_m^\ell,qquad
   255	 I_m^\ell=(1+\ell)+
   256	 \sum_{\sigma\in\mathcal P_m}(\delta_\sigma-1-\ell).
   257	\]
   258	
   259	So the frozen report's shifted Theorem 5.1, new \(I_m^\ell\), and shifted
   260	Corollary 5.3 are correct. In particular, a minor-free \(\ell=1\) child has
   261	\(I_m^\ell=2\), not 1. The sealed replay explicitly used 1 as a DATA
   262	convention for its minor column; that convention is not the shifted theorem.
